# ARM B of the quality-immunity check: the SAME suit, carrying AQ_FIRE_RES.
# The positive arm; quality-self-immune-plain.keys is the control (bd inc-to9x).
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/quality-self-immune-quality.keys 5
#
# BOTH HALVES OF THE RULING ARE MEASURED HERE.
#
# The ITEM half: wizard option 13, "Add Quality to Armour" (src/Debug.cpp:746),
# puts AQ_FIRE_RES on the worn suit. It draws no random number for an AQ_*
# value (QItem::AddQuality, src/Item.cpp:2919 onward walks straight to the
# Qualities array), so the two arms stay in step. Twelve fireballs must then
# leave the suit at 56 of 56 hit points, its numbers line must read
# "vs. Immune (leather)", and its hardness table must list Fire as an immunity.
#
# The WEARER half: the same quality still grants the wearer RESIST AD_FIRE of
# three per magical plus (lib/m_items.irh:645). The suit is +0 while it burns,
# on purpose -- see quality-self-immune-setup.keys for why the item half is
# only measurable at +0 -- so the grant is worth nothing until the fireballs
# are done. Two Scrolls of Enchant Armour then take it to +2, and
# Item::SetInherentPlus calls ReApply(), which re-runs the quality's EA_GRANT
# at the new plus. The sheet must then read "Fire 6".

@include quality-self-immune-setup.keys

# AQ_FIRE_RES on the worn suit. The prompt takes the constant's name, which
# src/Debug.cpp:758 looks up in AQ_CONSTNAMES.
w
@choose "Add Quality to Armour"
@expect "Enter Quality Constant"
"AQ_FIRE_RES"
ENTER
@until "Things in View" ESC

@include quality-self-immune-burn.keys

# --- the wearer half ----------------------------------------------------
# THE HELM COMES FIRST, because reading a scroll is a die roll and this
# measurement must not rest on one. Item::ReadScroll gates the whole effect on
# SkillCheck(SK_DECIPHER, 10 + sLevel) (src/Magic.cpp:3721). Enchant Armour is
# Level 3 and sLevel is Level*2-1 (src/Magic.cpp:3681), so the DC is 15, and
# this mage's Decipher rating is 2. SkillCheck rolls two d20 for SK_DECIPHER
# and keeps the better (src/Skills.cpp:1539), so a bare read lands about two
# times in three; a failed read prints "The magic runs amok!", spends the
# scroll, and leaves the suit's plus where it was.
#
# That is what took this fixture red on 2026-09-11. inc-19ay gave every breath
# weapon the dice its statblock declares, which moved the random stream from
# the first breath onward; the first of the two reads then landed on a failure,
# the suit finished at +1, and the sheet read "Fire 3". Nothing about the
# property had changed. Measured on the fixed build, seed 5: read one failed at
# "Decipher Script Check: 1d20 (10 [10/2]) +2 = 12 vs DC 15".
#
# "Comprehending Languages and Reading Magic" (lib/m_items.irh:5772) is a helm
# whose entire effect is SKILL_BONUS SK_DECIPHER +10. It takes the rating to 12
# against DC 15, so only a pair of ones and twos can fail a read now, and both
# reads below land on any ordinary stream. It grants no resistance of any kind,
# so it cannot touch what either half of this arm measures, and it goes on
# AFTER the burning and after the genocide, so it cannot reach the item half at
# all. Column 18 of the acquisition prompt is Helms (src/Tables.cpp:339); the
# extra DOWN selects the matched row, as it does for the suit in
# quality-self-immune-setup.keys. [q] is the Helmet slot and SPACE wears it.
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*18
@until "Comprehending Languages" DOWN
DOWN
ENTER
q
SPACE
@while "more --" SPACE
@until "Things in View" ESC

# Two ordinary Enchant Armour scrolls, +1 each. Column 1 of the acquisition
# prompt is Scrolls; the plain scroll is the row above "Enchant Armour
# (featherlight)", which is where @until leaves the cursor.
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT
@until "Enchant Armour (featherlight)" DOWN
ENTER
s
ESC
r
@choose "(in pack) Scroll of Enchant Armour"
@while "Stop reading?" n
@while "Select target or inventory item" *
@while "Die?" n
@while "more --" SPACE
@until "Things in View" ESC

w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT
@until "Enchant Armour (featherlight)" DOWN
ENTER
s
ESC
r
@choose "(in pack) Scroll of Enchant Armour"
@while "Stop reading?" n
@while "Select target or inventory item" *
@while "Die?" n
@while "more --" SPACE
@until "Things in View" ESC

# The suit's page again, now at +2 and carrying the quality by name.
@until "SPACE:Swap" i
@until ">>j)Armour" j
@until "base value of" x
@dump:quality-item
@until "Things in View" ESC

# The Resistances page: the wearer still gets what the quality always gave him.
d
@until "Resistances and Armour" DOWN
@dump:quality-sheet
@until "Things in View" ESC
@quit
